tasks.description:
Independent audit of Dongzhe (Denzel) Zheng's claimed proof of the Marcus-de Oliveira conjecture for n = 4 (preprint doi:10.13140/RG.2.2.36790.25923, 24 Oct 2026; public supplement github.com/DongzheZheng/The-Marcus-de-Oliveira-conjecture-for-n-4 pinned at commit 53ec16567d2307266ce52a8e9678410b2457cc27; paper PDF sha256 1f3dafad5021bbeff8b4a9cbc79de45846c47c7bfb1d542167e8a8c29aa1c138).

Deliverables, all under research/marcus-de-oliveira/zheng-n4-audit/:
(a) a dependency map of the proof: Theorem 1.2 (unitary to orthogonal), the contact reduction, the 82-facet and 214-orbit classification, and for each contact case T_1..T_90 the proof documents it depends on, with every dependence on a document labelled conditional traced to where its condition is discharged or left open;
(b) an independent re-derivation of the reduction from MOC(4) to the finite list of contact inequalities, with exact own-code replays of its finite parts;
(c) an independent replay of the exact checks case by case, with own code where feasible;
(d) a verdict per case (confirmed / gap found / could not check) with the evidence level, and an overall verdict stating exactly what is and is not established.

Acceptance: every verdict names what was checked and how, with reproducible commands; anything reported as established has been re-derived or re-run by a second pass that did not produce it; conjecture, computational evidence, written proof and independently checked proof are kept apart. A numerical non-violation is evidence, not a proof. The audit does not edit other lanes.
